# ruff format baseline — POLICY, hand-edited, never regenerated (#136).
#
# Nothing gated `ruff format` until #136, and the drift grew while a comment
# on that issue read the Prettier gate (#483) as the Python one: 90 files
# unformatted on 2026-09-12, 143 on 2026-10-06. Same contract as
# web/.prettier-baseline: `scripts/check_format_baseline.py` fails on a file
# that drifts without being listed here, AND on a listed file that has since
# been formatted. So this list can only shrink.
#
# What is still pinned, and why it was not simply reformatted:
#   src/      — Sonar scores reformatted lines as new code against its 80%
#               changed-line coverage gate; #229 failed at 64.9% doing all
#               of it at once. Take a file once its own coverage is >= 80%,
#               the way #465 did.
#   perseus/, scripts/ — coverage-excluded, but the files below carry
#               duplication Sonar reports (perseus/ as a whole: 9.9%), and a
#               reformat counts every duplicated line it touches against the
#               3% new-code duplication gate. scripts/generate_author_artifacts.py
#               carries an open Sonar BUG, which a reformat could re-attribute
#               as new and fail the reliability rating.
#
# To unpin: `.venv/bin/ruff format <path>`, delete its line, `make check`.

